From a10d8766fc34a1f6aceb516503a57b7ad7592ac3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Agent 1 <new@indusagi.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:18:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Agent 1] P15 wave 1: gateway models, routing, authorization,
 admission, outbound

- Fake chat platform with Telegram/Discord/Slack wire fakes and the shared
  adapter contract suite; gateway and platform config; inbound events;
  send result, error classifier and retry policy; adapter base with
  capability flags and per-chat send slots (P15-01..05).
- Platform registry, scoped token locks and proxy choice; one session key
  builder and the routing index; the authorization chain (fails closed),
  unknown-sender handling and mention gating; pairing (store in state/)
  and `indus pairing`; bot-loop guard, concurrency cap, admin tiers
  (P15-06..10).
- Admission pipeline with session claims, busy guards and busy-input
  modes, chat slash commands (P15-11..13).
- Chunker, platform formatters, stream consumer with typing and tool
  progress, outbound sender with forced redaction and dead targets, and a
  media path policy that only sends files from trusted places
  (media_trust_recent off by default) (P15-14..18).
- Deleting a session drops its gateway routes. D-16.238..253.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
